// REJECTS: Can't have config property with reserved name 'scopeElements'
//
// A FileGeneration body is `(scopeElements | generationOutputPath | configProperty)*`, and
// configProperty matches ANY `name: value;` -- including the two names that have dedicated
// rules. Give `scopeElements:` a scalar instead of the `[...]` array its own rule demands
// and the parser falls through to the generic arm, where the walker refuses it by name.
//
// This is a genuinely surprising interaction between an open-ended rule and a specific one:
// the grammar cannot express "these two names are taken", so the walker does, and a rewrite
// that keeps only the open-ended arm would accept a config property that shadows a real
// field.
###FileGeneration
Avro fixture::neg::ReservedConfigName
{
   scopeElements: 'fixture::neg::Person';
}
